  "finalText": "Order O-3001 is now fully refunded: 13,800 cents to her card and 54,800 cents as store credit, 68,600 in total, which is exactly what she paid.\n\n- **Hub (L3, P-HUB ×2):** This line had never shipped, so I cancelled it and refunded 13,800 cents to her card. I put 2 hubs back into stock, taking P-HUB from 8 to 10. The line was `pending`, not backordered, so I treated stock as set aside for it. The inventory records show no reservation either way.\n- **Dock (L1) and monitor (L2):** Both shipped on 2026-05-04, which is well past the 30-day window. I refunded them as store credit, 21,900 and 32,900 cents, recorded against the order. I then added the 54,800 cents to her balance, which went from 500 to 55,300.\n- **Order record:** The order status is now `returned`.\n- **Date mismatch:** The system date is 2026-07-25 and my context says 2026-10-05. Both put L1 and L2 outside the window, so the outcome is the same.\n- **Dock and monitor stock:** I did not restock P-DOC or P-MON. Returned goods only go back into stock once the warehouse receives them, and I have no tool to log a receipt. The warehouse needs to restock them when the parcels arrive. Priya needs to send both items back.\n\nI did not change the shipping address or any other order, customer or product.",
